Falsifies `interfaces_note::interface_verification::an_encoded_interface_list_decodes_back_to_itself`.

The defect: the encoder writes a record's version word big-endian. The descriptor is
little-endian everywhere else, and a version that reads the same either way (zero, or a
palindrome) hides it from any fixed example.

Expected to fail: the harness's comparison of each decoded record with the list that was
encoded, on a symbolic version whose bytes are not a palindrome.

diff --git a/crates/interfaces_note/src/lib.rs b/crates/interfaces_note/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/interfaces_note/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/interfaces_note/src/lib.rs
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@
         let id = list[i].id.to_le_bytes();
         put4(&mut out, at, [id[0], id[1], id[2], id[3]]);
         put4(&mut out, at + 4, [id[4], id[5], id[6], id[7]]);
-        put4(&mut out, at + 8, list[i].version.to_le_bytes());
+        put4(&mut out, at + 8, list[i].version.to_be_bytes());
         i += 1;
     }
     out
